 "text": "Marie Curie did something no one had done before. She won no bell prizes in two different sciences. In 1903, she shared the physics prize with Pierre Curie and Henry Beckwell for research on radiation. In 1911, she won chemistry for her work on radium and polonium. The lesson is not a motivational slogan. Look at how one line of research led her across the boundaries between subjects."
